      "type": "reading_card",
      "title": "Konglish — Korean + English",
      "title_kr": "콩글리시",
      "body": "Konglish (콩글리시) refers to English loanwords adapted into Korean pronunciation and sometimes with shifted meanings. Korea has adopted thousands of English words, making them sound Korean. The trick: if you know the English word, you can often guess the Korean by applying Korean pronunciation patterns — replace 'r' with 'ㄹ', add vowels between consonants, and end with a vowel.",
      "tip": {
        "icon": "🌐",
        "label": "Pronunciation key",
        "text": "English 'f' → ㅍ (p sound): file → 파일. English 'v' → ㅂ (b sound): video → 비디오. Final consonant clusters get a vowel: desk → 데스크, style → 스타일. Once you know the pattern, hundreds of words unlock instantly!"
      },
      "body_ja": "コングリッシュ（콩글리시）は英語の外来語を韓国語の発音に合わせて取り入れたものです。意味がずれる場合もあります。韓国語は英語から数千の単語を取り入れており、韓国語らしく聞こえます。コツ：英語の単語がわかれば韓国語の発音ルールを当てはめて推測できます―「r」はㄹに、子音の間に母音を入れ、語末に母音を付ける。",
      "tip_ja": {
        "label": "発音の鍵",
        "text": "英語の「f」→ㅍ（p音）：file→파일。「v」→ㅂ（b音）：video→비디오。語末の子音クラスターには母音を加えます：desk→데스크、style→스타일。パターンを覚えれば何百もの単語が一気に解錠されます！"
      }
    },
